# REQUIRES: python-api, cuda
# The correction for the dispersion of the Python model on a GPU
# (D[python-dispersion]): a pair term's own `dispersion` and an explicit
# correction, against mdir run and the tails of check_pair_tail.py.
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/pair_tail_system.py %t 60 60 32 3.7 0.5
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_dispersion.py %t GPU mdir | FileCheck %s
# CHECK: GPU Double cutoff: potential, virial and pressure of default, explicit, term, optout, off equal to mdir run's rows
# CHECK: GPU Double cutoff: the term's energy beyond the cutoff
# CHECK: GPU Double shift: the term's virial beyond the cutoff
# CHECK: GPU Mixed shift: the term's pressure beyond the cutoff
# CHECK: diverges: refused when asked for
# CHECK: no cell, switch: as the control file; by default a switch turns the correction off with a warning
# CHECK: tunable exponent: taken by a term left out
# CHECK: python dispersion passed
